950→### Reading Color Attributes via UV Lookup [[Ep8, 54:40](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KJUZD4PTyz0&t=3280s)]
951→```vex
952→i@primid;
953→v@uv;
954→f@dist;
955→
956→@dist = xyzdist(1, @P, @primid, @uv);
957→
958→@P = primuv(1, 'P', i@primid, @uv);
959→
960→@Cd = primuv(1, 'Cd', i@primid, @uv);
961→```
962→Using xyzdist to find the closest primitive and UV coordinates on a grid, then using primuv to read both position and color attributes from that location. This allows points elevated above a grid to sample and adopt the color values from their nearest primitive below.
